From: Gran Turismo 6 for Mac <https://github.com/Wooloomooloo2/Gran-Turismo-6-Mac>
Subject: [PATCH] page-fault waits detach and report, a destroyed queue is forgotten; 337 answers a refused map; Verify's marks order; Open2's checks

Upstream: not yet submitted; written to be upstreamed (generic, no title names)
Licence: MIT, as ps3recomp (see its LICENSE); offered under the same terms
Base: ps3recomp 4e8f3ca87a3e1d87bb83b8b7e9348fe2685cd514 (after 0001-0034)

What (fixes to 0029, 0033 and 0034, from their review, M-1 to M-6 and M-8):
- M-1: a host thread (no PPU identity) that goes on because the page was
  mapped for another thread leaves its slot "detached" until the pager's 57
  for its own still-queued event arrives, so that 57 answers CELL_OK as lv2
  answers it for a suspended thread (it answered EINVAL). A detached slot is
  taken first: its event was sent first.
- M-2: a thread waiting on a page fault prints a "still waiting" line every
  5 s, for PPU and host threads.
- M-4: sys_event_queue_destroy tells the page-fault areas (through a hook
  sys_mmapper_pf.c sets, so builds without it still link); an area whose
  queue is gone stops the process on its next fault instead of sending the
  event to a queue that reused the id. lv2 disconnects the notification's
  event port.
- M-5: 337 (search_and_map) answers ps3_mm_map's error instead of OK.
- M-3: cellPamfVerify also refuses an unknown block that starts before the
  end of the marks (libpamf's order check, as RPCS3 models it; an unknown
  offset of 0 with marks set is refused too).
- M-6: cellDmuxOpen2 checks the callback function and each field of the
  CellDmuxResource or CellDmuxResourceEx it carries, as libdmux does.
- M-8: the 1 ms retry interval is named as RPCS3's choice.
Behaviour reference: RPCS3 sys_mmapper.cpp, Thread.cpp, cellPamf.cpp and
cellDmux.cpp (GPL-2.0, read only, no code from them).
Tests: tests/test_mmapper_page_fault.c (PPU-served-first ordering, a
destroyed queue whose id is reused), tools/test_loader_memory_domain.py (a
refused map), tests/test_pamf_header_dmux.c (marks order, Open2).

